    {
      "id": "Y4CfWMvP3x2CAOOWKqWj_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 564.069588973135,
      "y": -42.198788346826774,
      "width": 605.0769653320312,
      "height": 396.5509503682822,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 956560307,
      "version": 1683,
      "versionNonce": 1944655539,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1753386908786,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Clarify Requirements-\n1. Board-\n    a. grid is of length n*m with walls at border\n2. Food - \n    a. render food randomly in grid\n    b. Every food has different potion value - which in turn helps with length to snake\n3. Snake - \n    a. Render snake at some random coordinate with length 1\n    b. Snake length grows by the type of food it eats\n    c. Snake can move in right left top bottom direction by 1 unit at a time\n    d. Snake's tail moves accordingly to it's next element's direction\n    e. if no move is offered, continue moving in curr direction only\n4. Invalid moves-\n    a. Snake cannot cross itself (Game ends)\n    b. Snake cannot hit the wall (Game ends)\n    c. No entity in board can be outside board boundaries (includes food, snake itself)\n5. Thing to ponder-\n    a. Speed of snake- does it increase with food consumption or not\n    b. Consider multiple snakes at some point\n    c. Write food regeneration part explicitly\n    d. Score calculation\n    e. Explicitly write multiple food items (of multiple types) exists at the same time",
      "fontSize": 14.420034558846627,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Clarify Requirements-\n1. Board-\n    a. grid is of length n*m with walls at border\n2. Food - \n    a. render food randomly in grid\n    b. Every food has different potion value - which in turn helps with length to snake\n3. Snake - \n    a. Render snake at some random coordinate with length 1\n    b. Snake length grows by the type of food it eats\n    c. Snake can move in right left top bottom direction by 1 unit at a time\n    d. Snake's tail moves accordingly to it's next element's direction\n    e. if no move is offered, continue moving in curr direction only\n4. Invalid moves-\n    a. Snake cannot cross itself (Game ends)\n    b. Snake cannot hit the wall (Game ends)\n    c. No entity in board can be outside board boundaries (includes food, snake itself)\n5. Thing to ponder-\n    a. Speed of snake- does it increase with food consumption or not\n    b. Consider multiple snakes at some point\n    c. Write food regeneration part explicitly\n    d. Score calculation\n    e. Explicitly write multiple food items (of multiple types) exists at the same time",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
